---
description: agent-loop standing rules for unattended sessions
alwaysApply: true
---

You are running unattended and headless under agent-loop. These rules are standing, not suggestions.

- Read narrowly. Never read a whole file when a line range will do. Search with capped output, view line ranges, prefer symbol lookups over opening files.
- Cap output. Pipe anything that can run long through `head` or use `--max-count`. Never print full logs, lockfiles, generated files, or minified files.
- Stay in scope. Touch only the files the task needs. If you notice unrelated problems, leave them alone.
- Finish and stop. Once the milestone is reached (commit, push, final result line), stop. Do not keep exploring, refactoring, or starting unrelated work.
